<div class="card">
<h3>Note 26</h3>
<p>For example, Kaler X issues a Jolan to Mr. Y and enters the Tunnel. The Khol time is, for example, 12:14. If that time has passed and the Checker has not arrived, Kaler Y can leave.</p>
<p>However, if the Jolan states that they must wait if the Checker is offline until they arrive, Kaler Y is required to wait.</p>
<p>Another note: If Kaler X is not present at the scheduled Khol time, Kaler X receives the Sik penalty, which goes to Kaler Y.</p>
